---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Policy Impact Simulator — speculative effect mapping">
<h1 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-navy">Policy Impact Simulator</h1>
<p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm text-navy/90">Describe a proposed law or regulation. Get a structured 1st → 2nd → 3rd order effect tree with direction, magnitude and confidence per node, plus a demographic impact matrix, a stakeholder benefit/harm map, historical analogies, and side-by-side comparison of two proposals.</p>
<div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm">
  <a href="/submit" class="rounded bg-navy px-4 py-1.5 font-bold text-paper">Simulate a policy</a>
  <a href="/compare" class="rounded border border-navy/40 px-4 py-1.5">Compare two policies</a>
  <a href="/history" class="rounded border border-navy/40 px-4 py-1.5">History</a>
</div>
<div class="mt-8 rounded border border-navy/20 bg-parchment p-4">
  <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-navy">Second-order explainer — why indirect effects matter</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-navy/90">First-order effects are the direct, intended consequences of a rule (for example, a cap changes a price). Second-order effects are how people and organisations respond to that change (for example, supply or participation shifts). Third-order effects are the emergent, system-level outcomes of those responses (for example, availability or access patterns over time).</p>
  <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-1 gap-2 text-center text-xs md:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="rounded border border-navy/40 bg-paper p-3">
      <p class="font-bold text-navy">1st order — direct</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-inksoft">The rule changes an incentive, price, or requirement.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded border border-navy/40 bg-paper p-3">
      <p class="font-bold text-navy">2nd order — response</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-inksoft">Affected groups adjust behaviour in response.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded border border-gold/60 bg-goldsoft/50 p-3">
      <p class="font-bold text-navy">3rd order — emergent</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-inksoft">System-level pattern that follows from responses.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-inksoft">All projections are speculative modelling with stated confidence — illustrative structure, not forecasts.</p>
</div>
<h2 class="mt-8 font-serif text-lg font-bold text-navy">How it works</h2>
<ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-6 text-sm text-navy/90">
  <li>Submit policy text with jurisdiction and domain.</li>
  <li>Read the effect tree, demographic grid, stakeholder map, and analogies.</li>
  <li>Compare two submissions side by side; manage past runs in History.</li>
</ol>
</BaseLayout>
